{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3060","artifact_type":"feature-context","name":"plan/feature-context-runtime-hints-r7-regroom.md@sha256:3e8d9c69c5e14c4545590fb674facf1ff2ea9ce511a47151a7bd694814836490"},"owner_reference":"3060","content":"# Feature Context: backlog_view runtime hints comply with R7 (re-groom, 2026-09-19)\n\n## Document Metadata\n\n- **Generated**: 2026-09-20\n- **Input Form**: artifact (backlog item #3060 entries plus the repo owner's comments)\n- **Source**: #3060 Acceptance Criteria 13.3, RT-ICA Final 2.7, Impact Radius 7.4, Research 11.1 (and 11.0 for the `next_call` convention), Dependencies 8.2. Repo owner comments dated 2026-09-19T06:59:44Z, 13:50:21Z and 14:14:22Z. PR #3649 diff.\n- **Code baseline**: `origin/main` at `d547db370064b4dafc865de987895f9102a231ef` (fetched 2026-09-20).\n- **Supersedes**: `plan/feature-context-runtime-hints-r7.md` (2026-08-20). The 2026-08-20 architect artifact `plan/architect-runtime-hints-r7.md` left an (a)/(b)/(c) mechanism choice open. The owner has since decided it: `map=True`.\n- **Status**: DISCOVERY_COMPLETE\n\n---\n\n## Original Request\n\nTitle: \"fix: runtime hints steer agents away from paginated navigation.\"\n\nDescription (#3060): \"The runtime strings that tell an agent what to call next steer it away from paginated navigation. The compact response's hint recommends loading full content as its first suggestion. The over-budget response tells a caller to request sections individually \u2014 advice a caller who already narrowed to one oversized section has exhausted. Neither mentions the paginated navigation parameters. Agents follow these strings. Documentation is a weaker lever: these are read on every call, at the moment of the decision.\"\n\nThe authoritative scope is the eight acceptance criteria in entry 13.3, restated as outcomes in Goals below.\n\n---\n\n## Core Intent Analysis\n\n### WHO (Target Users)\n\n- **Agents that call `backlog_view`**: every dh agent and skill that reads a backlog item through the MCP tool, in any harness. Examples are groomers, fact-checkers, impact analysts and orchestrators. They read `_hint` and `_usage` at the moment they choose the next call.\n- **The repo owner.** Grades the item against R7 and owns the #3054 rollout, which #3060 blocks (Dependencies 8.2).\n- **Downstream maintainers of #3057 and #3059.** Their work changes the fields and mechanisms these hints can name.\n\n### WHAT (Desired Outcome)\n\nAt the moment an agent decides its next call, the runtime strings do three things:\n\n1. They lead with a narrower read, not a full-content load (R7 prohibition 1).\n2. They do not re-offer narrowing the caller has already done (R7 prohibition 2).\n3. They state honestly where the recommended next step can still fail. The `map=True` route is not bounded until #3059 lands.\n\nThe tool's own schema description (`summary` parameter) carries the same order: scoped read first. The fix counts as done only when it is on `origin/main`. A plan reporting complete is not enough.\n\n### WHEN (Trigger Conditions)\n\n- **T1**: an agent calls `backlog_view(selector=X)` with the default `summary=True` and gets the compact manifest with `_hint`.\n- **T2**: an agent calls `backlog_view(selector=X, summary=False, section=<one section>)` or passes `sections=[one]`, and that single section is still over the 4,000-token budget. The agent gets `_over_budget: true` with `_usage`.\n- **T3**: an MCP client lists or inspects the tool schema before any call and reads the `summary` parameter description.\n\n### WHY (Problem Being Solved)\n\nAgents follow the hint strings literally. On `origin/main` today:\n\n- `_hint` leads with an unscoped `summary=False` load, which violates R7 prohibition 1. See `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2101-2104`.\n- `_usage` gives the same section-narrowing advice unconditionally, even to a caller who already narrowed to one section. That violates R7 prohibition 2. See `server.py:2176-2184`, and the signature at `server.py:2147`, which carries no narrowing state.\n\nA caller in T2 has no named way forward. It retries a call it has already made, or falls back to reading everything. Both waste context, and a fallback to a full read can exceed the harness response cap. The `summary` schema text (`server.py:2270`) also puts full content first, so the same bias is taught before any call. Plan `Pe6bcc5c2` reported 100% complete while none of its work was merged. That is a process failure this re-groom also guards against, through AC 8.\n\n---\n\n## Codebase Research\n\n### Similar Patterns Found\n\n#### Pattern 1: `next_call` continuation hint (EXTRACT mode)\n\n- **Location**: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/disclosure_handler.py`, `_handle_extract()` next_call construction. Research 11.0 cites it around lines 484-490. That is an August citation and was not re-verified on this pass.\n- **Relevance**: the R7-compliant precedent. It is conditional (set only when `truncated`), a single call you can paste as-is, and computed from the current response's state.\n- **Reusable**: the convention: conditional, one call, state-derived.\n\n#### Pattern 2: `next_call` in `backlog_list` and in `sam_schema` `_paginate_results()`\n\n- **Location**: `backlog_core/server.py` `backlog_list()` and `sam_schema/server.py` `_paginate_results()`. Research 11.0 cites them; they were not re-verified on this pass.\n- **Relevance**: two more sites confirm that a continuation hint is emitted only when a next step exists.\n- **Reusable**: same convention as Pattern 1.\n\n#### Pattern 3: the drafted fix on PR #3649 (open, `mergeable: CONFLICTING`)\n\n- **Location**: branch `fix/3060-r7-hints`, commits `a90ed1e06` and `dc5b6d264`. It changes `backlog_core/server.py`, `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py`, `backlog_core/tests/test_view_over_budget_gate.py`, and the three `plugin.json` manifests.\n- **What it does**, read from `gh pr diff 3649` on 2026-09-20:\n  - It reorders `_hint`: section narrowing first, full load second. That meets AC 1.\n  - It adds a keyword-only `narrowed_to_single_section` flag to `_build_over_budget_view`. `backlog_view` sets the flag when `section`/`sections` was passed and exactly one section remains in `full_response[\"sections\"]`.\n  - When the flag is set, `_usage` reads: \"...even after narrowing to a single section \u2014 further section= narrowing is not available for this request. Get this item's ordinal map, then page through the oversized section with navigate=/head=/skip_tokens=:\\n  backlog_view(selector='...', map=True)\". That meets AC 2.\n- **Gaps against 13.3**: the PR has **no statement that `map=True` may exceed the budget on a large item** (AC 3) and **no change to the `summary` Field description** (AC 5). The owner's 14:14:22Z decision confirms that plan `Pe6bcc5c2` has no task for AC 3 or AC 5.\n- **Reusable**: the owner directs the regenerated plan to start from the #3649 branch.\n\n### Existing Infrastructure\n\n- `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_000` (`server.py:231`).\n- The callers of both builders sit inside `backlog_view`: `server.py:2513` calls `_build_over_budget_view` and `server.py:2520` calls `_build_compact_manifest`.\n- `_sections_index_from_result()` (`server.py:2112`) emits a bracket `[N] Title (count)` index. That is not the dot-path ordinal scheme `navigate=` resolves (`docs/component-architecture.md:44-48`; #3057 removes it).\n- The MAP builder is unbounded. `disclosure_handler.py:396` does `map_text = \"\\n\".join(mapper.format_map_line(e) for e in entries)`, and `over_budget` at `:402` is diagnostic only.\n- **Live observation, this session**: `backlog_view(selector=\"#3060\", map=True)` returned `over_budget: true` with `total_est_tokens: 44722`. The owner-approved narrowed route can already produce an over-budget MAP on this item.\n\n### Code References\n\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2068`: `_build_compact_manifest`, with `_hint` at 2101-2104\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2147`: `_build_over_budget_view`, with `_usage` at 2176-2184\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2264-2273`: `summary` Field description, \"...and _hint showing how to load full content or specific sections\"\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md:1223`: remaining-ownership debt row listing `#3060` (AC 6 requires it to stay)\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md:1219, 1285`: MAP is complete but unpaginated (#3059)\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md:158-163`: R7 text\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/disclosure_handler.py:387-402`: MAP response assembly\n\n---\n\n## Use Scenarios\n\n### Scenario 1: default read of a large item (T1, maps to AC 1)\n\n**Actor**: a grooming agent\n**Trigger**: calls `backlog_view(selector=\"#N\")` with the default `summary=True`\n**Goal**: read only the sections it needs\n**Expected Outcome**: the first call `_hint` suggests is section-scoped. The full load is at most a later alternative.\n\n### Scenario 2: narrowed read still over budget (T2, maps to AC 2, 3, 4)\n\n**Actor**: a fact-check agent that already asked for one section (for example `section=\"Impact Radius\"`)\n**Trigger**: gets `_over_budget: true` because that one section exceeds 4,000 tokens\n**Goal**: reach that section's content\n**Expected Outcome**:\n- `_usage` does not tell it to narrow by section again.\n- `_usage` names `backlog_view(selector=..., map=True)`.\n- The same text states that `map=True` may itself exceed the budget on a large item.\n\nThe full outcome, where the agent gets the section content with no response over budget, is owned by #3059 and not by this item (owner decision, 13:50:21Z).\n\n### Scenario 3: schema read before any call (T3, maps to AC 5)\n\n**Actor**: an MCP client or agent inspecting tool schemas\n**Trigger**: lists tools\n**Goal**: learn how to read an item cheaply\n**Expected Outcome**: the `summary` description lists a section-scoped read before a full-content read.\n\n### Scenario 4: close-out verification (maps to AC 6, 7, 8)\n\n**Actor**: the orchestrator or repo owner at `/dh:verify-done`\n**Trigger**: the plan reports complete\n**Goal**: confirm the item is actually done\n**Expected Outcome**:\n- The five named test files pass (exit 0).\n- The change is on `origin/main`.\n- `ARCHITECTURE.md:1223` still lists #3060 while any criterion is unmet.\n\n---\n\n## Gap Analysis\n\n### Identified Gaps\n\n| # | Category | Gap Description | Impact |\n|---|----------|-----------------|--------|\n| 1 | Behavior | The drafted `_usage` narrowed text (PR #3649) does not state the `map=True` budget limit | AC 3 unmet. Agents treat `map=True` as safe; this item's own MAP is 44,722 est. tokens and `over_budget: true` |\n| 2 | Behavior | The `summary` Field description is still full-content-first on main and on #3649 | AC 5 unmet; the bias is taught before every call |\n| 3 | Integration | PR #3649 is `CONFLICTING` with main. It also bumps three `plugin.json` manifests | AC 8 (merged to main) cannot pass until the conflict is resolved. The version bumps are the probable conflict source; this was not verified |\n| 4 | Behavior | The drafted narrowed `_usage` names `navigate=/head=/skip_tokens=` in prose, but the over-budget response carries no field for them | Matches AC 4's recorded caveat (R7 prohibition 3 unmet pending #3059). A design question remains: does naming them in prose help or add a new violation? See Q2 |\n| 5 | Scope | AC 2 covers only the single-section case. A caller that narrowed to several sections (`section='0,1'`) and is still over budget gets the generic advice again | The generic advice is still actionable there (narrow further, down to one section), so this is probably not an R7 violation. The criteria do not state it either way. See Q3 |\n| 6 | Behavior | `_hint`'s section option tells callers to pass `section='<index...>'` using the bracket `[N]` index, which #3057 will remove | When #3057 lands, the hint text can name an address scheme the response no longer carries (prohibition 3). This is not a #3060 criterion. RT-ICA 2.7 condition 6 says the reorder does not depend on #3057 |\n| 7 | Integration | Plan `Pe6bcc5c2` is stale. The owner directs regeneration via `dh:add-new-feature` from the #3649 branch | A planner that reuses the old plan misses AC 3 and AC 5 |\n| 8 | Integration | Dependencies 8.2's \"Blocks\" line still says \"because PR #3642 has not merged\". #3642 is closed and replaced by #3649 | Stale pointer in the item; low impact |\n\n---\n\n## Questions Requiring Resolution\n\nThe owner's 2026-09-19 decisions settle every user-decision question. What remains is design work for the architect.\n\n### Q1: Wording and placement of the `map=True` limit statement (AC 3)\n\n- **Resolution Channel**: architect-research\n- **Category**: Behavior\n- **Gap**: The owner decided that the limit is recorded \"in the `_usage` hint text\" (13:50:21Z). The exact wording is open.\n- **Question**: Word the limit in `_usage` so it is observable to a test and does not steer the agent into a guaranteed over-budget call. Also decide whether it should name #3059, or name a recourse for when MAP is over budget. Candidates: `summary=False` with `section=` plus the head/skip route; the MAP response's own `over_budget` flag.\n- **Why It Matters**: AC 3 is the only new behavior not drafted on #3649.\n- **Resolution**: _pending_\n\n### Q2: Should the narrowed `_usage` name `navigate=/head=/skip_tokens=` in prose?\n\n- **Resolution Channel**: architect-research\n- **Category**: Behavior\n- **Gap**: The user's PR #3649 text says \"page through the oversized section with navigate=/head=/skip_tokens=\". R7 prohibition 3 forbids naming a mechanism absent from the response. The response has no such field, but the recommended `map=True` call returns the ordinals `navigate=` needs. The `next_call` precedent (`disclosure_handler.py` `_handle_extract`) emits one call that can be pasted as-is, with no multi-step prose.\n- **Question**: Evaluate whether naming the follow-on parameters is consistent with R7 and the `next_call` convention, or whether `_usage` should name only `map=True` and leave the follow-on to the MAP response. AC 4 already records prohibition 3 as unmet, so either choice passes 13.3. The question is quality, not scope.\n- **Why It Matters**: it avoids adding a second prohibition-3 exposure that #3059 would then have to unwind.\n- **Resolution**: _pending_\n\n### Q3: Multi-section narrowed callers still over budget\n\n- **Resolution Channel**: architect-research\n- **Category**: Scope\n- **Gap**: The PR #3649 flag fires only when exactly one section remains. With two or more, the generic \"request them individually\" advice returns.\n- **Question**: Confirm that this is R7-compliant, because the caller can still narrow to one section. Also decide whether a test should pin it so the boundary is explicit.\n- **Why It Matters**: it keeps the fix from being read as covering more (or less) than AC 2 states.\n- **Resolution**: _pending_\n\n### Q4: Resolving the #3649 merge conflict and manifest version bumps\n\n- **Resolution Channel**: architect-research\n- **Category**: Integration\n- **Gap**: #3649 is `CONFLICTING`. It touches `.claude-plugin/`, `.codex-plugin/` and `.cursor-plugin/` `plugin.json`.\n- **Question**: Identify the conflicting hunks and follow the repo's version-bump convention when rebasing onto main. See `/rebase` pre-analysis.\n- **Why It Matters**: AC 8 requires the change on `origin/main`.\n- **Resolution**: _pending_\n\n### Q5: `summary` description wording (AC 5)\n\n- **Resolution Channel**: architect-research\n- **Category**: Behavior\n- **Gap**: `server.py:2270` reads \"_hint showing how to load full content or specific sections\".\n- **Question**: Reword it so a section-scoped read is listed first and it stays accurate about the `[N]` index that #3057 will remove. Also check whether any test or doc snapshot pins this description string.\n- **Why It Matters**: this text reaches every caller before any call is made.\n- **Resolution**: _pending_\n\n---\n\n## Goals (Pending Resolution)\n\n1. The compact manifest's hint leads an agent to a section-scoped read before any full-content read (AC 1).\n2. An agent that narrowed to one section and is still over budget is not re-told to narrow by section. It is directed to the owner-approved `map=True` call (AC 2).\n3. That same direction tells the agent honestly that `map=True` may exceed the budget on a large item (AC 3).\n4. The item's own record states that R7 prohibition 3 is unmet for the narrowed hint pending #3059, and does not claim otherwise (AC 4, already true in Dependencies 8.2).\n5. The tool's schema description teaches a scoped read before a full read (AC 5).\n6. #3060 stays listed as open debt in `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` until every other criterion holds (AC 6).\n7. The named test files pass, and the change is merged to `origin/main` (AC 7, AC 8).\n\nOut of scope, per owner decisions:\n- The end-to-end \"gets the section content without any over-budget response\" outcome belongs to #3059.\n- The five agent files that call `summary=False` directly belong to #1161.\n- Removing the bracket index belongs to #3057.\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. Architect resolves Q1-Q5 against the #3649 branch as the starting point.\n2. Regenerate the plan with `dh:add-new-feature` against entry 13.3 (owner decision, 14:14:22Z).\n3. Refresh Dependencies 8.2's stale \"#3642 has not merged\" line to name #3649.\n"}